window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Tarian lost her for eight hundred years. He won’t let her go again.</b></p> <p>Kenna Murillo’s biggest concern should be passing organic chemistry—not the dragon shifter who crashes into her life, furious, half-feral, and swearing she belongs to him.</p> <p>But Tarian has spent centuries imprisoned, cursed to live without the one soul who was always meant to be his. Now he’s free—and so is she. Only, the ones who killed her previous incarnations? They never stopped hunting. And this time, they don’t just want her dead. They want to unmake her.</p> <p>Kenna can deny the past. She can fight the pull between them. She can run.</p> <p>Or she can stand beside the dragon who would burn everything down—except her.</p>"; 
